walking the closed-form null curve in three fuel landscapes
(dchi2 near zero means the curve is still a null direction)

                fuel field          +5%        +10%        +20%        +30%  control +30%
                   uniform        -0.95        0.31       -0.95        0.17        222404
   gradient (0.65 - 1.35x)         0.05        0.15       -0.16       -0.06        201066
        rough random (2:1)         0.02       -0.02        0.03        0.01        203578

  worst dchi2 anywhere on the curve, any landscape: 0.95 (1 sigma = 1)
  smallest control value (same wind error, no compensation): 201066
  ratio: 210955x

  The degeneracy is unchanged by fuel heterogeneity, as the algebra requires:
  a constant rescaling of the whole field is exactly the null direction, and
  that holds whatever the field looks like.

  Not covered: a fuel field whose *shape* is unknown. That adds unknowns
  without adding mask observables, so it can only make matters worse.

